@startuml alert-lifecycle
!include style.iuml
title Alert and delivery lifecycle

state "Alert" as alert {
  [*] --> open : first matching event\n(alert_created)
  open --> open : identical event in the dedup window\ncount + 1
  open --> acknowledged : operator acknowledges
  open --> resolved : manual · source_resolved · silence
  acknowledged --> resolved : manual · source_resolved
  resolved --> [*]
}

state "Delivery (one per recipient and channel)" as delivery {
  [*] --> pending : outbox relayed\n(channel already chosen by routing\nand working hours)
  pending --> delivered : channel accepted
  pending --> failed : send error
  failed --> delivered : retry succeeds
  failed --> dead_lettered : retry or outage budget spent\n→ fallback channel queued
  dead_lettered --> delivered : replay_dead_letters.py
  delivered --> [*]
}
note bottom of alert
  Grouping is separate from dedup: different events of one rule
  inside a window send one group summary instead of N messages.
end note
@enduml
